Fixed. 

**The bug:** `src/sim.ts:43` — `if (foodSurplus >= 0)` — grew population whenever surplus was zero or positive, so a settlement that merely matches food production to consumption (surplus = 0) kept growing.

**The fix:** changed to `if (foodSurplus > 0)`, so population grows only on an actual surplus.

Verified: `npm run test` (4/4 pass) and `npm run typecheck` (clean).


